//
// /*******************************************************************//**
// PURPOSE: This is simple curve/curve coincidence checker.
//   Finds 1a. CurveEndPoint/OtherCurve points of coincidence and
//         1b. OtherCurveEndPoint/Curve points of coincidnece
//         2. Intervals of coincidence between those points of coincidence
//         3. Breaks Intervals into pieces at minima points
//
// NOTES:
//     It assumes that neither curve is closed and that the curves
//     are flat enough to drop points locally.  This routine is primarily
//     used by other routines which have already done all of the
//     subdivision and stuff to assure that things are well behaved.
//
// METHOD ---
//     The Curve/Point minDistances are found for all 4 Curve endPoints.
//     and solutions sorted by ThisCurve parameter values.  Solutions
//     are generated for the 1st and last solution values as
//     1. No Solutions - return rlNumFound = 0
//     2. 1 Solution   - return rlNumFound = 1, 1 SINGLE_VALUE solution
//     3. 2 or more Solutions
//        3a. when maxDistance between curves over 1st/last solution segment
//            is greater than d3dTolerance,
//                       return rlNumFound = 2, 2 SINGLE_VALUE solutions
//        3b. When minDistance between Curves over 1st/last solution segment
//            is less than endPoint Solutions/2,
//            Split interval at minPoint and
//                       return rlNumFound = 2, 2 RANGE_OF_VALUE solutions
//        3c. when maxDistance < d3dTolerance and minDistance is
//            not less than endPoint distances,
//                       return rlNumFound = 1, 1 RANGE_OF_VALUE solution.
// ***********************************************************************/
