// /*******************************************************************//**
// PURPOSE: This is a cheap global curve/curve coincidence checker.
//     It's designed to detect the case where all of one curve is
//     coincident with another.  It also detects cases where curve end-points
//     bound regions of partial coincidence.  When partial or no coincidence
//     is detected one must intersect the regions of non-coincidence
//     to find the complete list of intersections.
//
// NOTES: The only coincidences it finds are ones which are
//                  bounded by the end points of the curves.
//     It will find complete curve coincidences,
//                  overlapping partial curve coincidences,
//                  coincidences where one curve is inside of the other,
//                  and closed curve coincidences.
//     When rbAdditionalWorkNeeded is set to true, one must inspect the returned
//                  solutions and call the global intersector on those regions of the
//                  curves which are not found to be coincident to complete the
//                  set of curve/curve intersections.
//
// METHOD ---
//     Drops the end points of each curve to the other.  When any
//     of the drop distances are less than 3ddTolerance, it checks
//     for and returns when appropriate a coincident interval.
//
//     When coincident solutions do NOT span all of one curve or the other,
//     then rbAdditionalWorkNeeded is set to TRUE so additional intersections
//     can be found.
// ***********************************************************************/
