// /*******************************************************************//**
// PURPOSE: This is a cheap global curve/curve coincidence checker.
//     It's designed to detect the case where all of one curve is
//     coincident with another.  However, it does find some, but not
//     all, cases of partial coincidence.  When partial or no coincidence
//     is detected one must intersect the regions of non-coincidence
//     to find the complete list of intersections.
//
// NOTES: The only coincidences it finds are ones which are
//                  bounded by the end points of the curves.
//     It will find complete curve coincidences,
//                  overlapping partial curve coincidences,
//                  coincidences where one curve is inside of the other,
//                  and closed curve coincidences.
//     It can miss or under-report a partial coincidence where one curve starts
//                  off coincident with the other and then diverges.
//                  Partial  coincidences can be under-reported because
//                  closed curves are processed recursively as subdivided
//                  segments.  Those artificial segmentation points get examined
//                  as end-points and a pair of curves which start off
//                  coincident and then diverge can be found coincident
//                  up to the segmentation point, not to the point of divrgence.
//     When rbAdditionalWorkNeeded is set to true, one must inspect the returned
//                  solutions and call the global intersector on those regions of the
//                  curves which are not found to be coincident to complete the
//                  set of curve/curve intersections.
//
// METHOD --- when the curves are not closed (or half closed), drops the
//     end points of each curve to the other.  When two or more of the end-point
//     drop distances are less than d3dTolerance, it checks for and returns
//     when appropriate a coincident interval.
//     When the curves are closed (or half closed) divides the curve into
//     three parts and recursively calls GlobalCoincidenceChecker() on the pieces
//     and reassembles the results.
//
//     When the coincident solutions do NOT span the entire curve, then
//     rbAdditionalWorkNeeded is set to TRUE so additional intersections
//     can be found.
// ***********************************************************************/
